Concern: re-running one block of a step from a restored residual, after its ops have run, in both trunk architectures
Upstream: not-submitted

The replay needs one thing from radiance that the issue observer (0101) does not give: a way to run
one block of the step alone, after its caller restored the residual at every boundary. It sets the
block on the engine, the architecture reads rad_replay_block() at the top of step() and issues only
that block between its brackets, and the observer, which runs after each op, hands the caller that
op's bytes before the planner reuses the buffer. The patch adds no observer of its own: 0101 has the
one call. Both trunk architectures honour the block: the bf16 arch, and the int8 trunk behind
qwen35_w8a8, whose replay takes the serial single-layer path with the serial brackets and never the
pipelined one.
